# The 3D verification itself: triangulate every direction both cameras detected,
# fit the planes, and report how far off the result is.
#
# This is what the dialog's "Start Calculation" runs. Every part of it -- the
# triangulation, the plane fit, the reprojection -- is computed here. The client
# receives numbers to print and images to show.
#
# No images are uploaded: the sources and their detections are already on the
# server, put there by Measure3dSource and DetectCheckerboard. What the request
# carries is the part that is not a measurement -- the numbers the operator typed.

# Where the two fisheyes are, in millimetres. These come from the dialog's spin
# boxes because nothing measures them: the baseline between the cameras is the
# one quantity the entire triangulation scales with, so it is an input, and a
# wrong entry here produces a 3D result that is internally consistent and the
# wrong size.
float64[3] cam_left
float64[3] cam_right

# Inner corner counts per direction, parallel arrays. Used for the grid edges in
# the plane fit; a direction absent here is still triangulated, just not drawn
# with its grid.
string[] directions
int32[] pattern_cols
int32[] pattern_rows
---
bool success

# Triangulated points as JSON: [{"dir":"north","pts":[[x,y,z], ...]}, ...] in
# millimetres, plus the two camera centres:
#   {"cam_left":[x,y,z], "cam_right":[x,y,z], "directions":[ ... ]}
#
# The client's GL view draws these. Drawing them is not computing them -- the
# view rotates a point cloud it was handed, and derives no measurement from it.
string points_json

# The four read-out rows the dialog fills in, per direction:
#   {"angle":{"north":12.3, ...}, "mean_dist":{...},
#    "plane_dist":{...}, "depth":{...}}
string metrics_json

# Reprojection drawn back onto each fisheye, one per camera, for the result tabs.
sensor_msgs/CompressedImage[] overlays
string[] overlay_labels

# Directions that were skipped because only one camera saw them. Named, because
# a quietly missing direction moves the plane fit without ever looking wrong.
string[] skipped

string message
